@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Operations";
    ViewData["OperationsSection"] = "home";
}

<div class="lu-kafka">
<partial name="_BackButton" model="@(new BackLink("/Home", "Dashboard"))" />
<h1 class="h3 mt-3">Throughput and scaling</h1>
<p>Kafka health, and the changes that start as a preview. Nothing moves until a later request is approved and executed.</p>
<partial name="_Nav" />
<div class="au-card card mt-3">
    <div class="card-header">Kafka</div>
    <div class="card-body">
        <p>Start with Overview when something looks wrong. Messages reads one allow-listed topic and does not commit offsets. Use Topic, Consumers, or Brokers when you already know what you want to change.</p>
        <ol class="lu-kafka-steps">
            <li>Overview lists topics and groups that need attention. Healthy tables stay folded.</li>
            <li>Messages shows a page of records. Export writes an audit of that read.</li>
            <li>Topic previews an in-place partition increase. Migrate is the other path, and it recreates the topic empty.</li>
            <li>Consumers previews adding or removing replicas. Brokers previews a decommission or a rebalance.</li>
        </ol>
        <a class="btn btn-au-link" asp-action="Kafka">Open Kafka</a>
    </div>
</div>
</div>
